$10,000 you have given year in and year out,

00:22:41.430 --> 00:22:45.060
uh, to help aquatics here in the city of Huntsville,

00:22:45.310 --> 00:22:47.220
more specifically at the shower center.

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:49.400
Uh, how many years you've been doing this?

00:22:52.140 --> 00:22:52.390
10.

00:22:54.970 --> 00:23:01.600
15 years she has been giving money faithfully to uh to the city of Huntsville

00:23:01.600 --> 00:23:04.310
to be applied at the uh Richard Shower Center,

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:07.280
uh, the aquatics program and tell us a little bit about that.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:09.710
Thank you, mayor and members.

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:13.970
The purpose of the funding is really to make sure those children who do

00:23:13.970 --> 00:23:17.830
not know how to swim have an opportunity to learn how to swim.

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:23.550
And I must say the staff at the shower center is certainly an amazing staff

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:28.260
in terms of their patience and their love for their job and also making

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:32.260
sure that our children have an opportunity to be able to swim because we

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:36.500
find that if you look at the statistics, especially in the African and American

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:40.260
community, we always have this challenge of a child dying.

00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:42.280
Uh, because they drowned.

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:45.150
I had a cousin when I was 12 that that happened to,

00:23:45.280 --> 00:23:47.460
so I learned to swim at age 30.

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:50.280
So if I figure if I can learn to swim at age 30,

00:23:50.520 --> 00:23:52.310
the child should have a much better time.

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:55.440
So thank you for the opportunity, and we look forward.

