Mr.

00:41:54.880 --> 00:41:58.630
Davis is here to make a presentation and then we will open the hearing.

00:42:00.240 --> 00:42:01.150
Thank you Madam President.

00:42:01.240 --> 00:42:03.540
Shane Davis, director of Urban Economic Development.

00:42:04.040 --> 00:42:05.510
Uh, good evening council members.

00:42:05.560 --> 00:42:08.060
You may recall the last city council meeting,

00:42:08.520 --> 00:42:12.740
uh, you passed a resolution, uh, directing the administration to,

00:42:13.200 --> 00:42:15.380
uh, come back and present you a proposed,

00:42:15.560 --> 00:42:16.030
uh.

00:42:16.870 --> 00:42:18.380
TIF project plan.

00:42:18.700 --> 00:42:22.200
Uh, this project plan would be in Limestone County portion of the annex

00:42:22.290 --> 00:42:23.030
Huntsville.

00:42:23.490 --> 00:42:27.440
Uh, so we've been working, uh, for about 3 weeks to put this draft plan

00:42:27.440 --> 00:42:31.000
together and tonight we're proud to present it to you and the general public.

00:42:33.080 --> 00:42:37.030
So much like uh the recent tip for downtown I do want,

00:42:37.120 --> 00:42:40.510
uh, especially for the public's sake to just quickly give a little bit of

00:42:40.510 --> 00:42:42.670
background on TI increment financing.

00:42:43.470 --> 00:42:47.810
Uh, since 2000, uh, the city of Huntsville has been very successful in establishing

00:42:47.810 --> 00:42:52.580
tax increment financing districts as permitted by Alabama law to finance

00:42:52.580 --> 00:42:54.230
public infrastructure projects.

00:42:55.100 --> 00:42:57.230
Um, the principle is very simple.

00:42:57.460 --> 00:43:02.820
Uh, you take future property tax revenues in a defined district,

00:43:03.140 --> 00:43:05.810
so think of property that is not currently developed,

00:43:05.900 --> 00:43:08.290
but as it develops it creates a new tax base.

00:43:08.380 --> 00:43:11.920
A new tax base would fund public infrastructure.

00:43:12.310 --> 00:43:17.100
Uh, that public infrastructure is put in ahead of time to induce or to entice

00:43:17.100 --> 00:43:18.170
that private investment.

00:43:18.970 --> 00:43:21.440
Uh, we get routinely asked with the general public,

00:43:21.490 --> 00:43:22.580
is this a tax increase?

00:43:22.650 --> 00:43:24.580
It is absolutely not a tax increase.

00:43:24.690 --> 00:43:28.600
The millage rate, uh, that you pay in Huntsville stays the same.

00:43:29.010 --> 00:43:33.800
Uh, that actually has to go by vote of the people to change property taxes.

00:43:33.930 --> 00:43:38.270
So this is just the way we would use those future property taxes,

00:43:38.690 --> 00:43:40.480
uh, to fund public infrastructure.

00:43:41.150 --> 00:43:45.860
Uh, lastly, the existing tax base within that district continues to go to

00:43:45.860 --> 00:43:49.780
the tax recipients as they do today, so we're not taking any existing revenue

00:43:49.780 --> 00:43:54.540
away from our general fund, uh, in this case the Limestone County General

00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:58.730
Fund, or any of the school systems within this tax district,

00:43:58.830 --> 00:44:01.550
so they'll continue to get whatever they got last year.

00:44:01.990 --> 00:44:06.580
Uh, it will be any future revenues that would be created as a result of

00:44:06.580 --> 00:44:07.540
this infrastructure.

00:44:08.310 --> 00:44:13.180
I do want to point out this, uh, proposed TI 8 district is different than

00:44:13.180 --> 00:44:13.860
some of the others.

00:44:13.990 --> 00:44:19.100
This would be our 3rd district under the major 21st century manufacturing

00:44:19.100 --> 00:44:19.380
Act.

00:44:20.200 --> 00:44:26.950
Uh, TI 6 and 7 TI 6 has closed, um, was the first 21st century,

00:44:27.180 --> 00:44:31.830
uh, manufacturing zone TI district, uh, the Mazda Toyota manufacturing,

00:44:31.920 --> 00:44:36.030
uh, project, uh, brought before you in the Limestone County Commission TI

00:44:36.120 --> 00:44:42.940
7, that is active, uh, and really move the needle out there with public

00:44:42.960 --> 00:44:45.180
infrastructure and roads and utilities and,

00:44:45.320 --> 00:44:46.040
and the things.

00:44:46.630 --> 00:44:50.730
And through those two TIF districts what we have created out in that area

00:44:50.790 --> 00:44:55.860
is over $3 billion of private investment that's now on the tax rolls and

00:44:55.860 --> 00:44:57.550
over 14,000 new jobs.

00:44:58.560 --> 00:45:02.500
So the proposed TIF 8 district district would be created under the Major

00:45:02.500 --> 00:45:07.110
21st century Manufacturing Zone Act, and the TIF 8 district would designate,

00:45:07.310 --> 00:45:10.880
uh, for the future Eli Lilly project that's recently announced and would

00:45:10.880 --> 00:45:12.890
get under construction sometime next year.

00:45:13.310 --> 00:45:18.620
Uh, that would be our designated manufacturing zone under this act with

00:45:18.620 --> 00:45:20.270
the TIFF you've got to designate.

00:45:20.500 --> 00:45:23.800
A manufacturing zone and and we'll get into that momentarily.

00:45:24.810 --> 00:45:26.760
So let's get into the actual project plan.

00:45:26.850 --> 00:45:29.660
Just wanted to provide that background, the differences,

00:45:29.770 --> 00:45:31.040
and also the general public.

00:45:31.130 --> 00:45:34.590
This is nothing about any type of tax increase,

00:45:35.050 --> 00:45:36.110
uh, to anyone.

00:45:37.740 --> 00:45:40.930
So the project area you can see kind of dashed in the in the black dashed

00:45:40.930 --> 00:45:45.280
area and and shaded in the in the the light shading will consist of just

00:45:45.340 --> 00:45:46.810
over 9000 acres.

00:45:46.940 --> 00:45:52.290
This will be very similar in size to TI 7 that that we uh did that's to

00:45:52.290 --> 00:45:55.910
the north and and actually goes all the way to uh 65.

