01:20:10.770 --> 01:20:11.550
Good evening.

01:20:12.090 --> 01:20:13.360
My name is Susan Higgins.

01:20:13.450 --> 01:20:16.640
I live at 1127 Nocust Avenue in Huntsville.

01:20:16.840 --> 01:20:17.160
Thank you.

01:20:17.370 --> 01:20:23.750
I wanna first thank Council Member Meredith for introducing Ordinance 26836

01:20:24.250 --> 01:20:26.230
to remove the tax on hearing aids.

01:20:26.600 --> 01:20:29.830
It's much appreciated, and I hope that all of City council will support

01:20:29.830 --> 01:20:30.170
this.

01:20:31.180 --> 01:20:33.820
I've been wearing hearing aids since I was 5 years old.

01:20:34.220 --> 01:20:38.840
I won't tell you my age, but I'd suffice it to say that's decades of experience.

01:20:39.340 --> 01:20:41.740
For most of our time, I wore two hearing aids,

01:20:41.940 --> 01:20:44.250
so it was double the cost and double the tax.

01:20:45.200 --> 01:20:47.400
Hearing loss is incredibly isolating.

01:20:47.920 --> 01:20:52.470
People with hearing loss rely on hearing aids and other technology to be

01:20:52.470 --> 01:20:55.090
independent and to participate in their communities,

01:20:55.320 --> 01:20:59.460
to work, to go to school, and to testify at city council meetings.

01:20:59.960 --> 01:21:03.500
For most of us, a hearing aid is not a luxury or a want.

01:21:03.760 --> 01:21:06.750
It is a fundamental necessity for quality of life.

01:21:08.140 --> 01:21:10.690
Hearing aids last about 3 to 5 years on average,

01:21:10.780 --> 01:21:12.830
so they're not a long-term investment.

01:21:13.340 --> 01:21:17.770
Many people with hearing loss experience decline over time,

01:21:17.900 --> 01:21:21.140
so replacements are needed sooner than that 5-year frame.

01:21:21.620 --> 01:21:25.160
Hearing aids are not covered by Medicare and most insurance companies.

01:21:25.500 --> 01:21:28.600
It's an out of pocket expense and is in this case,

01:21:28.620 --> 01:21:29.410
it's taxed.

01:21:30.000 --> 01:21:33.510
They range in price from $99 to over $8000.

01:21:34.410 --> 01:21:36.770
I just ordered a new hearing aid on Tuesday.

01:21:37.170 --> 01:21:40.240
It will cost me $1950.

01:21:41.210 --> 01:21:45.970
The tax on that is $78 and that's small in terms of the bigger price,

01:21:46.250 --> 01:21:49.150
but it's also a big strain, especially these days.

01:21:49.650 --> 01:21:52.840
I am paying a tax for something I fundamentally need.

01:21:53.450 --> 01:21:54.440
There's no choice.

01:21:55.550 --> 01:21:58.410
If I want to be independent and participate in my community,

01:21:58.910 --> 01:22:02.220
this is the only hearing aid that works with the technology that I need.

01:22:03.480 --> 01:22:07.140
For many in our community, you are relieving them of a tax burden of between

01:22:07.160 --> 01:22:12.710
$20.40 dollars, a small loss of revenue for the city and a major relief

01:22:12.710 --> 01:22:16.380
for many of our citizens who are retired or on limited incomes.

01:22:17.220 --> 01:22:21.210
We'd like each of you to consider that continuing this tax you are taxing

01:22:21.210 --> 01:22:25.490
an item that is absolutely necessary and absolutely critical for some of

01:22:25.490 --> 01:22:27.000
our citizens.

01:22:27.270 --> 01:22:31.450
It is certainly enough of a budget consideration that next time I'll drive

01:22:31.450 --> 01:22:35.480
up to Madison City to buy hearing aid, but they have repealed the tax.

01:22:36.190 --> 01:22:38.090
Many cities across the state are doing this,

01:22:38.180 --> 01:22:40.160
and I hope that Huntsville would be a leader.

01:22:40.700 --> 01:22:41.460
Thank you so much.

01:22:42.370 --> 01:22:43.120
