01:27:19.680 --> 01:27:22.430
Uh, one of the concerns I want to express,

01:27:22.720 --> 01:27:26.130
especially as we start, you know, pivoting into a new fiscal year,

01:27:26.560 --> 01:27:30.950
is, uh, what seems to have been a pattern which unfortunately had taken

01:27:30.950 --> 01:27:32.240
place in, um.

01:27:32.800 --> 01:27:36.030
Numerous streets, I think not just within the district I represent,

01:27:36.160 --> 01:27:39.940
but I think in other streets, uh, that were being resurfaced in other parts

01:27:40.160 --> 01:27:44.270
of the city, uh, there's a process where streets,

01:27:44.400 --> 01:27:47.740
for example, let me use Holiday Drive as an example,

01:27:48.080 --> 01:27:50.610
is prepped before resurfacing takes place.

01:27:50.680 --> 01:27:53.330
Uh, the contractor and the people come in,

01:27:53.480 --> 01:27:57.980
they kind of mill the, the asphalt down, they,

01:27:58.040 --> 01:28:01.070
uh, fix the curb and have everything all prepped up.

01:28:01.580 --> 01:28:06.850
And then there's a second contractor that comes in who basically takes over

01:28:06.850 --> 01:28:10.250
and does the fun part laying out the asphalt with the results that people

01:28:10.250 --> 01:28:11.180
like to see.

01:28:11.700 --> 01:28:15.000
There's been a process that's been a problem rather where,

01:28:15.300 --> 01:28:20.690
um, Holiday Drive, for example, spent at least 7 months where it was torn

01:28:20.690 --> 01:28:24.060
up and the residents on it had to live on it,

01:28:24.220 --> 01:28:28.610
go through the dust, slow down occasionally there'd be a windshield that

01:28:28.610 --> 01:28:30.250
would get hit with the pea gravel.

01:28:30.690 --> 01:28:35.460
And they would have to wait and we would still not get a satisfactory response

01:28:35.460 --> 01:28:39.680
from the public works director about when the asphalt contractor would be

01:28:39.680 --> 01:28:40.220
coming.

01:28:40.940 --> 01:28:44.310
Uh, I'm using as an example, Harwood, uh,

01:28:44.410 --> 01:28:50.550
Holiday has a similar example, uh, had a long waiting period.

01:28:51.250 --> 01:28:56.400
Uh, Homewood Drive basically went through being milled in the fall and then

01:28:56.400 --> 01:29:00.080
not being resurfaced until the, uh, wintertime came.

01:29:00.760 --> 01:29:03.800
Eustace, it's still like a work in progress,

01:29:04.000 --> 01:29:08.110
but I'd like to see if there's some way we can either get with this public

01:29:08.110 --> 01:29:12.870
works director or whoever takes charge to have something lined up where

01:29:12.870 --> 01:29:18.750
the contractors know and they are bound by contract and whatever it takes

01:29:18.750 --> 01:29:22.760
to make it happen where there's a reasonable period of time where.

01:29:23.140 --> 01:29:27.800
The prepping is done and then after the prepping is done shortly thereafter

01:29:27.800 --> 01:29:29.820
the asphalting would take place.

01:29:30.170 --> 01:29:32.630
Uh, by contrast, I hate to say this, but,

01:29:32.650 --> 01:29:37.080
uh, in our backyard over here on Church Street we had something similar

01:29:37.080 --> 01:29:41.840
where it was milled, it was prepped, and then very shortly after then the

01:29:41.840 --> 01:29:44.960
asphalt, uh, would come in and that would,

01:29:45.050 --> 01:29:48.640
you know, minimize the inconvenience that the citizens had to go through,

01:29:48.770 --> 01:29:49.000
but.

01:29:49.360 --> 01:29:50.510
I think this is a problem.

01:29:50.640 --> 01:29:54.350
