02:20:22.150 --> 02:20:24.740
Um, essentially it's quite simple.

02:20:24.830 --> 02:20:28.130
I could either pay TVA for that power or I could pay our customers for that

02:20:28.150 --> 02:20:28.540
power.

02:20:29.000 --> 02:20:30.310
And I'd rather pay the customer.

02:20:30.640 --> 02:20:34.670
And so the rate that the customer gets paid is based on our current TVA

02:20:34.670 --> 02:20:35.190
rates.

02:20:35.870 --> 02:20:38.130
And so no customers being subsidized.

02:20:38.390 --> 02:20:41.660
No customer has to worry that certain solar customers are getting a deal

02:20:41.660 --> 02:20:42.870
that other customers aren't.

02:20:43.150 --> 02:20:44.180
It's the same energy.

02:20:44.270 --> 02:20:47.290
I would just rather pay our customers for it than pay TVA for it.

02:20:47.430 --> 02:20:51.390
Is it, um, I know in some parts of the country,

02:20:51.790 --> 02:20:55.740
um, I think it's called plug-in solar where they can just get it,

02:20:55.870 --> 02:20:56.380
plug it in.

02:20:56.460 --> 02:21:01.430
And somehow miraculously what they're pulling down goes into your system,

02:21:01.570 --> 02:21:04.360
is that going to happen or is that a different program?

02:21:04.410 --> 02:21:05.800
We're still talking about that.

02:21:05.890 --> 02:21:11.320
So this rooftop solar program has a, has an inspected interconnection.

02:21:11.610 --> 02:21:14.710
So the electrical inspector checks and makes sure that everything is wired

02:21:14.710 --> 02:21:16.990
up right and the disconnects are safe.

02:21:18.200 --> 02:21:20.670
We have a little anxiety with just plug-in solar.

02:21:20.720 --> 02:21:24.110
A lot of electric utilities do because we had an electric employee a number

02:21:24.110 --> 02:21:28.870
of years ago who was badly hurt and burned in electrocution because we thought

02:21:28.870 --> 02:21:30.050
the circuit was off.

02:21:30.240 --> 02:21:31.990
The customer had a generator running.

02:21:32.080 --> 02:21:34.530
It was providing power back through the power line,

02:21:34.760 --> 02:21:37.070
and our employee burned his arm very badly.

02:21:37.880 --> 02:21:39.350
And so, um.

02:21:39.820 --> 02:21:40.930
We're very sensitive to that.

02:21:40.980 --> 02:21:44.170
We want to make sure that there's proper safety protocols associated with

02:21:44.170 --> 02:21:44.600
that.

02:21:44.860 --> 02:21:47.590
With this rooftop solar program, we have that in place.

02:21:47.920 --> 02:21:51.930
We need to think carefully about how we implement a more diverse program.

02:21:52.060 --> 02:21:52.880
It sounds great.

02:21:52.910 --> 02:21:57.000
Thank you, and I understand your concerns regarding the plug-in makes perfect

02:21:57.020 --> 02:21:57.460
sense.

