I support investing in our public servants,

03:07:16.490 --> 03:07:22.320
but if we can find room in our budget to address compensation,

03:07:22.730 --> 03:07:27.620
we should bring that same urgency to affordability for our residents.

03:07:28.990 --> 03:07:34.690
Tonight, we're finally considering eliminating the city sales tax on something

03:07:34.710 --> 03:07:36.730
as essential as hearing aids.

03:07:37.110 --> 03:07:42.940
So I would highly recommend um thinking about that more clearly.

03:07:43.200 --> 03:07:47.660
We're also considering another 236 acres for annexation,

03:07:47.750 --> 03:07:52.660
a new tax increment financing district, and more than 800 acres moving through

03:07:52.660 --> 03:07:55.260
major zoning and rezoning actions.

03:07:56.080 --> 03:08:00.620
When we annex land to create a TIF district or rezone hundreds of acres,

03:08:00.840 --> 03:08:03.790
we aren't just moving lines on a map.

03:08:04.780 --> 03:08:07.050
We're adding people, infrastructure demands,

03:08:07.100 --> 03:08:10.530
and long-term obligations that outlast any single vote.

03:08:10.820 --> 03:08:14.890
Residents deserve to see the math before decisions are finalized,

03:08:15.220 --> 03:08:15.890
not after.

03:08:17.980 --> 03:08:20.930
And if we're inviting newcomers to the Star of Alabama,

03:08:21.060 --> 03:08:23.320
we should welcome them as Huntsvillians.

03:08:24.650 --> 03:08:28.890
But we also cannot forget the people who already built their lives here.

03:08:29.850 --> 03:08:34.310
Developers benefiting from our growth should be held to their commitments.

03:08:34.450 --> 03:08:38.960
Growth should not leave residents and taxpayers carrying the consequences

03:08:39.440 --> 03:08:43.080
because ultimately this comes back to representation.

03:08:44.460 --> 03:08:49.760
No elected official, no candidate, no institution is above the voters.

03:08:50.340 --> 03:08:53.320
The polling place belongs to the voters.

03:08:54.690 --> 03:08:56.790
City Hall belongs to the people.

03:08:57.930 --> 03:09:04.920
And public office belongs to the people, not the person temporarily entrusted

03:09:04.920 --> 03:09:05.480
with it.

03:09:05.960 --> 03:09:09.180
Huntsville's grown, Huntsville has grown tremendously.

03:09:09.770 --> 03:09:14.000
Now our representation, accountability, and capacity have to grow with it.

03:09:14.840 --> 03:09:15.860
I'll give you back your time.

03:09:16.040 --> 03:09:16.600
Thank you.

03:09:18.730 --> 03:09:19.080
Thank you.

03:09:19.130 --> 03:09:21.420
And finally we will hear from Harold Kemp.

03:09:22.580 --> 03:09:23.050
Is Mr.

03:09:23.220 --> 03:09:24.050
Kemp still here?

03:09:25.790 --> 03:09:26.540
He is not.

03:09:26.670 --> 03:09:27.820
That was our last speaker.

03:09:27.920 --> 03:09:30.220
Then do we have a motion to adjourn?

03:09:30.670 --> 03:09:31.140
Motion for Mr.

03:09:31.270 --> 03:09:31.540
Little.

03:09:31.670 --> 03:09:32.250
Thank you.

03:09:32.480 --> 03:09:33.660
Uh, thank you, council members.

03:09:33.750 --> 03:09:37.840
We'll see you, uh, for the work session on September 18th at 11 o'clock.
